      "leaked": [
        {
          "pid": 3151,
          "ppid": 10463,
          "comm": "bash",
          "cmdline": "bash -c cd /home/Raymer/work_space\necho \"=== soak \u8fdb\u5ea6 ===\"\ntail -12 /tmp/soak-run.log 2>/dev/null | sed 's/^/  /'\necho\necho \"=== \u63d0\u4ea4 defconfig \u6ce8\u91ca\u4fee\u6b63 ===\"\ncd um/repo/src\ngit add arch/um/configs/arm64_defconfig\ngit -c user.name=Raymer8639 -c user.email=diliyangemail@gmail.com commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\num: correct what the 16 KB default is justified by\n\nThe defconfig explained CONFIG_PAGE_SIZE_16KB with \"Android 15 and later ship\n16 KB kernels\". That is not true, and the phone this port is developed against\nis the counterexample: a Redmi 23124RN87C on Android 15 (SDK 35) reports 4 kB,\nfrom KernelPageSize in /proc/self/smaps, and the 16 KB guest boots and runs\nthere -- the full network gate passes on it, recorded in\ndocs/evidence/2026-10-16-umnet-network.json.\n\nThe setting itself is still right, for a reason that does not depend on the\nversion number: the constraint only points one way. A 4 KB guest cannot boot on\na 16 KB host; a 16 KB guest boots on either. So 16 KB remains the default, and\nthe comment now says that instead of repeating a claim a device can falsify.\n\nNo functional change.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1",
          "starttime": 81860862,
          "rss-kb": 3540,
          "in-gate-tree": true
        }
